        "original_id": "a13f5d98-26d6-5f29-9ceb-1544fe4e7c46",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sangin, Lashkargah, Afghanistan, Sistan Basin\n- Water systems: Helmand River\n- Infrastructure: Route 611\n\nFacts:\n- The Helmand River is the longest river in Afghanistan and the primary watershed for the endorheic Sistan Basin.\n- Sangin is located in the valley of the Helmand River at an altitude of 888 meters and lies 95 kilometers northeast of Lashkargah.\n- Route 611 in Afghanistan is approximately 100 kilometers long and passes through the town of Sangin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
